Applications of DFS (Depth First Search):

1. Finding connected components in a graph.
2. Detecting cycles in a graph.
3. Topological sorting of a directed acyclic graph (DAG).
4. Finding paths between two vertices.
5. Solving mazes and puzzles.
6. Finding connected regions in a grid.
7. Detecting whether a graph is connected.
8. Finding strongly connected components.
9. Finding articulation points and bridges.
10. Backtracking problems such as N-Queens.
11. Checking whether a graph is bipartite.
12. Performing graph traversal and tree traversal.
